analysis:
Examined base_text units for docs/provider/cli-reference.md lines 1227-2134 (stop/restart/status/doctor/verify/models/benchmark/update/autoupdate/beta/fan/login/logout/enroll/unenroll/local/logs/report/watchdog/exit codes). These are unchanged base excerpts. The PR's changed head ranges (743-747, 751-769, 1852, 1859-1860) are documentation only. Per the patch excerpt, they add `darkbloom update --rollback` and `--yes`. The new text says rollback restores the retained predecessor and quarantines the installed release. It also says rollback contacts no coordinator, swaps the layout through the watchdog's journaled rollback under the update lease, drains, then restarts. Code is in provider-swift/Sources/darkbloom/UpdateRollback.swift, which was not supplied.

Security relevance: an operator-initiated downgrade relates to T-043 (watchdog rollback authority is the same replaceable binary), T-054 (unqualified or revoked signed build accepted through stale code evidence) and T-013/T-034. ADV-001 already controls local binaries, so a documented local rollback is not by itself a new trust grant. Serving authorization (A-016/A-017, TB-011) should still require coordinator qualification of the restored build. Doc lines 1269 and 1281 indicate restart requires fresh App Attest, legacy or self_route authorization.

The head lines 1852 and 1859-1860 fall in the autoupdate/beta region. The head text was not supplied, and I identified no regression from the base context. No source-level evidence shows the rollback path bypassing hash verification or coordinator build qualification. I made no finding because the implementation is outside this batch.

Integration should verify these points in UpdateRollback.swift:
- the restored predecessor is integrity-checked (signature, CodeDirectory, metallib hashes) before activation;
- a release revoked by the coordinator is still refused authorization after rollback;
- the update lease and journal prevent races with the watchdog;
- `--yes` and noninteractive handling cannot be triggered by a non-owner.

The threat model (T-043/TB-003) may need a note on the explicit operator rollback command.
